---
import Layout from '../layouts/StandardLayout.astro';
import { currentSite } from '../lib/site';
const key = currentSite(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_KEY);
const agdrExample = `---
id: AgDR-0001
timestamp: 2026-02-04T12:00:00Z
agent: claude-code
model: claude-opus-4-5
trigger: user-prompt
status: executed
---

# Auth Provider for Serverless Chrome Extension

Chosen: AWS Cognito

Why: Native API Gateway integration and managed security.

Trade-off: Hosted UI limitations and AWS lock-in.`;
const orbitPlan = `PLAN REVISION 4

Outcome
Users authenticate through corporate SSO.

Acceptance
○ SSO login succeeds
○ Existing password sessions remain valid
○ Logout terminates both sessions`;
const orbitSnapshot = `PROJECT SNAPSHOT

web-app       main @ 81fee032
auth-service  main @ 4ed128ac

Current reality, captured before reconciliation.`;
const orbitReconciliation = `RECONCILIATION

✓ existing OAuth provider found
! previous auth assumption invalidated
+ one discovery deferred
→ next bounded change available`;
const interop = `{\n  \"rel\": \"implements\",\n  \"type\": \"orbit.execution-slice\",\n  \"id\": \"slice-004\"\n}`;
const orbitSlice = `EXECUTION SLICE

Configure the existing provider
for the corporate IdP.

Contributes to  AC-1
Based on       web-app @ 81fee032
               auth-service @ 4ed128ac`;
---
{key === 'agentsdlc' && <Layout><section class="page landing"><p class="pathbar">~/agentsdlc</p><p class="eyebrow">Agent SDLC</p><h1>Open artefacts for<br />agentic software engineering.</h1><p class="lede">Agents move between sessions, tools and repositories. Engineering intent and reasoning should survive them.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button quiet" href="#standards">See how Agent SDLC works ↓</a></div><div id="standards" class="standards-heading"><p class="section-label">STANDARDS</p></div><div class="standards-grid"><section class="standard editorial"><p class="section-label">STANDARD</p><p class="standard-name">ORBIT</p><h2>Keep execution aligned<br />with durable outcomes.</h2><p class="meta">Planning and Reconciliation Specification</p><p>Define intent and outcomes once. Reconcile them against current software reality. Materialise only the next bounded execution slice.</p><a href="https://orbitspec.dev">Explore ORBIT →</a><p class="meta">orbitspec.dev</p></section><section class="standard editorial"><p class="section-label">STANDARD</p><p class="standard-name">AgDR</p><h2>Record what the agent<br />decided and why.</h2><p class="meta">Agent Decision Record Specification</p><p>Preserve consequential technical decisions and rationale beyond the agent session that created the code.</p><a href="https://agdr.dev">Explore AgDR →</a><p class="meta">agdr.dev</p></section></div><section class="editorial"><p class="section-label">HOW THEY WORK TOGETHER</p><h2>Independent by design.<br />Composable when useful.</h2><p class="meta">INTEROPERABILITY</p><p>ORBIT determines what work is justified next. AgDR preserves why a consequential technical decision was made during that work.</p><p>Neither standard depends on the other.</p><pre class="code">ORBIT Plan
    ↓
Reconciliation
    ↓
Execution Slice
    ↓
Agent
 ├──→ Code
 └──→ AgDR</pre><pre class="code">{interop}</pre></section><section class="split"><div><p class="section-label">WHY AGENT SDLC</p><h2>Sessions disappear.<br />Engineering context should not.</h2><p>Agentic development creates useful context inside conversations, agent runs and prompts. Agent SDLC defines small durable artefacts for the parts that need to survive.</p></div><div class="contrast-rows"><div class="contrast-row"><b>Transient</b><b>Durable artefacts</b></div><div class="contrast-row"><p><strong>Conversation</strong><br />Useful while the session is active, but not a durable engineering record.</p><p><strong>ORBIT Plan</strong><br />Preserves intended outcomes.</p></div><div class="contrast-row"><p><strong>Agent session</strong><br />Ends when the run finishes or context resets.</p><p><strong>AgDR</strong><br />Preserves why a consequential technical decision was made.</p></div><div class="contrast-row"><p><strong>Runtime prompt</strong><br />Describes what the agent knew or was told at that moment.</p><p><strong>Evidence and execution provenance</strong><br />Can preserve what supported an assessment and which project state justified work.</p></div></div></section><div class="trust-strip"><b>OPEN BY DEFAULT</b><span>Versioned specifications</span><span>Machine-readable schemas</span><span>Public change history</span><span>Implementation-neutral contracts</span><a href="/governance">About Agent SDLC →</a></div></section></Layout>}
{key === 'agdr' && <Layout><section class="page landing"><p class="pathbar">~/agdr</p><p class="eyebrow">AgDR 1.2.0 · OPEN STANDARD</p><h1>Record what the agent decided<br />and why.</h1><p class="lede">AI agents make consequential technical choices during implementation. AgDR preserves the decision and its rationale after the session ends.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/quick-start">Adopt AgDR</a><a class="button quiet" href="#record">See an example</a><a class="button quiet" href="/specification">Read the specification</a></div><section id="record" class="editorial"><p class="section-label">THE RECORD</p><h2>A decision that survives the session.</h2><p>AgDR records the context, alternatives, decision and consequences of a consequential choice.</p><pre class="code">{agdrExample}</pre><p class="code-actions">Copy Markdown · View raw</p><p><a href="https://github.com/me2resh/agent-decision-record/blob/main/examples/AgDR-0001-auth-provider-choice.md">View source ↗</a></p></section><section class="editorial"><p class="section-label">ADOPT</p><h2>Use AgDR with the agent you already have.</h2><div class="rows"><p><b>Claude Code</b><span>Plugin or manual /decide command</span></p><p><b>Codex</b><span>Skill under <code>.codex/skills</code></span></p><p><b>Cursor</b><span>Always-on <code>.mdc</code> rule</span></p><p><b>GitHub Copilot</b><span>Repository instructions</span></p><p><b>Windsurf</b><span>Cascade rule</span></p><p><b>Any AI</b><span>System prompt instructions</span></p><p><b>Git + CI</b><span>Hooks and validator workflow</span></p></div><a href="/integrations">See installation paths →</a></section><section class="split"><div><p class="section-label">THREE FILES. ANY AGENT.</p><h2>Portable by default.</h2><p>AgDR does not require a plugin or proprietary runtime. Copy the template, schema and validator into any repository.</p><p><a href="/quick-start">Copy the setup →</a></p></div><pre class="code">agdr-template.md
       +
agdr.schema.json
       +
validate-agdr.js
       ↓
docs/agdr/AgDR-*.md</pre></section><section class="editorial"><p class="section-label">MACHINE CHECKABLE</p><h2>A standard the agent can fail.</h2><p>The repository validator checks metadata, enums, filename identity, required sections, Y-statements, unique IDs and supersession references.</p><pre class="terminal">$ node scripts/validate-agdr.js docs/agdr/*.md
✓ AgDR-0001 valid
✓ AgDR-0002 valid

2 records checked
0 errors</pre><p><a href="https://github.com/me2resh/agent-decision-record/blob/main/scripts/validate-agdr.js">View validator source ↗</a></p></section><section class="split"><div><p class="section-label">WHEN TO RECORD</p><h2>Record choices that change the system.</h2><p><b>Create an AgDR</b><br />Choose a library, architecture, storage model, migration strategy, security approach or lasting project convention.</p></div><div><p><b>Do not create an AgDR</b><br />Variable names, formatting, routine refactoring, existing conventions and straightforward fixes.</p></div></section><section class="split"><div><p class="section-label">ADR VS AGDR</p><h2>AgDR complements ADR.</h2></div><div class="comparison"><p><b>ADR</b><br />Human or team · design process · usually manual</p><p><b>AgDR</b><br />AI agent · during execution · metadata and automated checks</p></div></section><section class="editorial"><p class="section-label">REAL EXAMPLES</p><h2>Decisions from the repository.</h2><p>Authentication, data models, migration strategies, mobile architecture, release workflows and image loading.</p><a href="/examples">Browse examples →</a></section><section class="editorial"><p class="section-label">INTEROPERABILITY</p><h2>Independent by design.</h2><p>AgDR remains useful on its own. With ORBIT, a record can optionally reference the execution slice or outcome context where the decision was made.</p><a href="https://agentsdlc.ai/interoperability">Read the profile →</a></section></section></Layout>}
{key === 'orbit' && <Layout><section class="page landing"><p class="pathbar">~/orbit</p><p class="eyebrow">ORBIT v0.1 · DRAFT</p><h1>Keep execution aligned<br />with durable outcomes.</h1><p class="lede">Plan intent once. Reconcile against reality. Materialise only the next bounded change.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/adopter-guide">Adopt ORBIT</a><a class="button quiet" href="/schemas">View schemas</a></div><div class="lifecycle"><p class="section-label">00 / THE LOOP</p>{['PLAN|Durable intent', 'OBSERVE|Current project state', 'RECONCILE|What changed?', 'SLICE|What is justified next?', 'EXECUTE|'].map((step) => { const [name,desc] = step.split('|'); return <div class="stage"><b>{name}</b><span>{desc}</span></div> })}</div><section class="split artefact-grid"><div><p class="section-label">01 / PLAN</p><pre class="code">{orbitPlan}</pre></div><div><p class="section-label">02 / PROJECT SNAPSHOT</p><pre class="code">{orbitSnapshot}</pre></div><div><p class="section-label">03 / RECONCILIATION</p><pre class="code">{orbitReconciliation}</pre></div><div><p class="section-label">04 / EXECUTION SLICE</p><pre class="code">{orbitSlice}</pre></div></section><section class="editorial"><p class="section-label">05 / THE MODEL</p><h2>A Plan is not a backlog.</h2><p>Durable outcomes. Disposable work. ORBIT decides what change is justified next; execution systems decide how to operationalise it.</p><a href="/specification">Read the draft specification →</a></section><section class="split"><div><p class="section-label">06 / RABBIT-HOLE PROTECTION</p><h2>A discovery does not automatically become work.</h2><p>Classify discoveries as required, supporting, adjacent or unrelated. Only knowledge required for the active outcome may become current work.</p></div><pre class="code">discovery
   │
   ▼
required for active outcome?
   ├── yes → candidate current work
   └── no  → record and defer</pre></section></section></Layout>}
